===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|armaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|h₂erHmos||joint|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|arm|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|arm|lang=osx}}, Dutch {{term|arm|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|arm|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Arm|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|armr|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|arm|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌰𐍂𐌼𐍃|tr=arms|lang=got}}. The [[Proto-Indo-European]] root is also the source of Old Church Slavonic {{term|рамо|tr=ramo|lang=cu}} (Russian {{term|рамо||tr=ramo|shoulder|lang=ru}}), Latin {{term|armus|lang=la}}.

